---@field propertyName? string The name of the property.
---@field freeShippingThreshold? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.FreeShippingThresholdList Conditions to be met for a product to have free shipping.
---@field salePriceEffectiveDate? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.Interval Date range during which the item is on sale, see [product data specification](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/7052112#price_and_availability).
---@field displayAdsId? string An identifier for an item for dynamic remarketing campaigns.
---@field pickupSla? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductAttributesPickupSlaEnum|string Item store pickup timeline. For more information, see [Pickup SLA](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/14635400).
---@field trim? string The [Trim](https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/14154176) of the vehicle model, such as `S`, `SV`, `SL` and others.
---@field energyEfficiencyClass? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductAttributesEnergyEfficiencyClassEnum|string The [energy efficiency class](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/7562785) as defined in EU directive 2010/30/EU.
---@field shortTitle? string The short title of the item.
---@field warranty? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.Warranty The [`warranty`](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/18562485) of the product.
---@field maximumRetailPrice? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.Price Maximum retail price (MRP) of the item. Applicable to India only.
---@field multipack? string The number of identical products in a business-defined multipack.
---@field minEnergyEfficiencyClass? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductAttributesMinEnergyEfficiencyClassEnum|string The [energy efficiency class](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/7562785) as defined in EU directive 2010/30/EU.
---@field includedDestinations? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductAttributesIncludedDestinationsItemEnumList The list of destinations to include for this target (corresponds to checked check boxes in Merchant Center). Default destinations are always included unless provided in `excludedDestinations`. For more information, see [Included destination](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/7501026). Note: We recommend setting destinations on datasources level for most use cases. Use this field within products to only setup exceptions.
---@field shipping? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ShippingList Shipping rules.
---@field minHandlingTime? string Minimal product handling time (in business days).
---@field sizeSystem? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductAttributesSizeSystemEnum|string System in which the size is specified. Recommended for apparel items. For more information, see [Size system](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6324502).
---@field shippingHandlingBusinessDays? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ShippingBusinessDaysConfigList The business days during which orders can be handled. If not provided, Monday to Friday business days will be assumed.
---@field propertyType? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductAttributesPropertyTypeEnum|string The type of property.
---@field latitude? number The latitude of the property. The value must be between -90 (inclusive) and 90 (inclusive), up to 6 decimal places.
---@field googleProductCategory? string Google's category of the item (see [Google product taxonomy](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/1705911)). When querying products, this field will contain the user provided value. There is currently no way to get back the auto assigned google product categories through the API.
