---@field customLabel1? string [Custom label 1](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6324473) for custom grouping of items in a Shopping campaign.
---@field vehicleAllInPrice? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.Price The all-in advertised price for a vehicle, which includes costs for the following – any accessories attached to the vehicle, environmental levies, extra warranty, fuel, freight, pre-delivery inspection (PDI), dealer fees for handling licensing, provincial regulatory fees, miscellaneous dealer charges for security etching and nitrogen tire fill, and factory-to-customer or dealer-to-customer discounts or incentives. See the [Vehicle all-in price](https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/14156981) for more information.
---@field utilitiesIncluded? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductAttributesUtilitiesIncludedItemEnumList The utilities included for the property.
---@field productFee? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductFeeList The product fee for the property.
---@field externalSellerId? string Required for multi-seller accounts. Use this attribute if you're a marketplace uploading products for various sellers to your multi-seller account.
---@field shippingLabel? string The shipping label of the product, used to group products in account-level shipping rules. Max. 100 characters. For more information, see [Shipping label](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6324504).
---@field color? string [Color](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6324487) of the item. For example, "red".
---@field vehicleMandatoryInspectionIncluded? boolean Whether the vehicle is sold with mandatory inspection and maintenance performed before delivery. See the [Vehicle mandatory inspection included](https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/15956630) for more information.`
---@field specialtyHousingType? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductAttributesSpecialtyHousingTypeEnum|string The specialty housing type for the property.
---@field condition? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductAttributesConditionEnum|string [Condition](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6324469) or state of the item.
---@field sizeTypes? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductAttributesSizeTypesItemEnumList The cut of the item. It can be used to represent combined size types for apparel items. You can provide up to two `SizeType` values, for example, `["PETITE", "MATERNITY"]` or `["BIG", "TALL"]`. For more information, see [Size type](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6324497).
---@field shippingLength? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ShippingDimension Length of the item for shipping.
---@field virtualModelLink? string URL of the 3D image of the item. See the [Help Center article](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/13674896) for more information.
---@field pickupMethod? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductAttributesPickupMethodEnum|string The [pickup](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/14634021) option for the item.
---@field unitArea? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.UnitArea The unit area of the property, such as `1000 sqft`.
---@field imageLink? string URL of an image of the item.
---@field petPolicy? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.PetPolicy The pet policy for the property.
---@field structuredTitle? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.StructuredTitle Structured title, for algorithmically (AI)-generated titles.
---@field engine? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductAttributesEngineEnum|string The [engine](https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/14156068) type of the vehicle.
---@field emissionsStandard? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductAttributesEmissionsStandardEnum|string The [emission standard](https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/14869021) of the vehicle.
---@field structuredDescription? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.StructuredDescription Structured description, for algorithmically (AI)-generated descriptions.
---@field numberOfUnits? string The number of units available for a specific floor plan of the property. The value must be greater than 0.
---@field numberOfBathrooms? number The number of bathrooms in the property. The value must be greater than 0 and a multiple of 0.5.
---@field subscriptionCost? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.SubscriptionCost Number of periods (weeks, months or years) and amount of payment per period for an item with an associated subscription contract.
---@field pattern? string The item's [pattern](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6324483). For example, polka dots.
---@field adult? boolean Set to true if the item is targeted towards adults.
---@field popularityRank? number Optional. Indicates the [popularity](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/17085297) of the product in a merchant's inventory. Using a scale of 0.0 (lowest) to 100.0 (highest).
---@field additionalImageLinks? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.StringList Additional URLs of images of the item.
---@field productHighlights? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.StringList Bullet points describing the most relevant [product highlights](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/9216100).
---@field numberOfBedrooms? number The number of bedrooms in the property. The value must be greater than or equal to 0 and a multiple of 1.0.
---@field productTypes? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.StringList Categories of the item (formatted as in [product data specification](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/7052112#product_category)).
---@field shoppingAdsExcludedCountries? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.StringList List of country codes [(ISO 3166-1 alpha-2)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_3166-1_alpha-2) to exclude the offer from Shopping Ads destination. Countries from this list are removed from countries configured in data source settings.
---@field material? string The [material](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6324410) of which the item is made. For example, "Leather" or "Cotton".
---@field documentLinks? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.StringList Optional. Contains a list of PDF [document URLs](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/17084656) for the product. Examples are training manuals, user guides, assembly instructions, package inserts, etc. Must start with "http://" or "https://"), ASCII characters only, and RFC 3986 compliant.
---@field loyaltyPoints? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.LoyaltyPoints Loyalty points that users receive after purchasing the item. Japan only.
---@field co2Emissions? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.Co2Emissions The [co2 emission](https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/14546146) of the vehicle.
---@field salePrice? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.Price Advertised sale price of the item.
---@field electricRange? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.Mileage The [electric range](https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/15162232) of the vehicle in miles/kms.
---@field link? string URL directly linking to your item's page on your online store.
---@field sustainabilityIncentives? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductSustainabilityIncentiveList The list of sustainability incentive programs.
---@field adsRedirect? string Allows advertisers to override the item URL when the product is shown within the context of Product ads.
---@field itemGroupTitle? string Optional. Represents the [title of the product group](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/17085146) to which this variant product belongs. This can be used along with the [item group id](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6324507) attribute. It lets you perform better grouping of variant products, and helps identifying common product characteristics more efficiently.
---@field price? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.Price Price of the item.
---@field minimumOrderValues? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductMinimumOrderValueList The [minimum value](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/16989009) in the cart before a customer can initiate checkout. Supports multiple minimum order values. Different minimum order values can be specified per country, service and surface. Maximum entries: 100.
---@field maxHandlingTime? string Maximal product handling time (in business days).
---@field relatedProducts? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.RelatedProductList Optional. Specifies how other [products are related](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/17085213) to this product.
---@field displayAddress? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.DisplayAddress The display address of the property.
---@field shippingWeight? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ShippingWeight Weight of the item for shipping.
---@field promotionIds? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.StringList The unique ID of a promotion.
---@field unitPricingMeasure? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.UnitPricingMeasure The measure and dimension of an item.
---@field autoPricingMinPrice? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.Price A safeguard in the [automated discounts] (https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/10295759) and "Dynamic Promotions" (https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/13949249) projects, ensuring that discounts on business offers do not fall below this value, thereby preserving the offer's value and profitability.
---@field carrierShipping? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.CarrierShippingList Rules for carrier-based shipping.
---@field brand? string [Brand](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6324351) of the item. For example, "Google".
---@field productHeight? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductDimension The height of the product in the units provided. The value must be between 0 (exclusive) and 3000 (inclusive).
---@field vehiclePriceType? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductAttributesVehiclePriceTypeEnum|string The [price type](https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/14592783) of the vehicle.
---@field returns? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ReturnsList Optional. [Return rules](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/17081382) for the product.
---@field isBundle? boolean Whether the item is a business-defined sub-API. A [sub-API] (https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6324449) is a custom grouping of different products sold by a business for a single price.
---@field questionsAndAnswers? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.QuestionAndAnswerList Optional. Contains user-, merchant-, and manufacturer-authored [questions and answers](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/17085211) about the product. Max 30 question and answer pairs. Max 10000 characters total. Each question can have max 1000 characters. Each answer can have max 1000 characters.
---@field gender? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductAttributesGenderEnum|string Target [gender](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6324479) of the item.
---@field availability? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductAttributesAvailabilityEnum|string [Availability](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6324448) status of the item.
---@field neighborhood? string The neighborhood (locality) of the property, such as `Wallingford`, `Greenwood`, etc.
---@field displayAdsValue? number Offer margin for dynamic remarketing campaigns. For more information, see [Display ads attribute](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6069387).
---@field excludedDestinations? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductAttributesExcludedDestinationsItemEnumList The list of destinations to exclude for this target (corresponds to unchecked check boxes in Merchant Center). For more information, see [Excluded destination](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6324486). Note: We recommend setting destinations on datasources level for most use cases. Use this field within products to only setup exceptions.
---@field installment? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductInstallment Number and amount of installments to pay for an item.
---@field expirationDate? string Date on which the item should expire, as specified upon insertion, in [ISO 8601](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) format. The actual expiration date is exposed in `productstatuses` as [googleExpirationDate](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6324499) and might be earlier if `expirationDate` is too far in the future.
---@field shippingTransitBusinessDays? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ShippingBusinessDaysConfigList The business days during which orders are in transit. If not provided, Monday to Friday business days will be assumed.
---@field size? string Size of the item. Only one value is allowed. For variants with different sizes, insert a separate product for each size with the same `itemGroupId` value, see [Size](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6324492).
---@field shippingWidth? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ShippingDimension Width of the item for shipping.
---@field model? string The [Model](https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/14154511) of the vehicle, such as `LX`, `EX`, and others.
---@field disclosureDate? string The date time when an offer becomes visible in search results across Google’s YouTube surfaces, in [ISO 8601](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601) format. See [Disclosure date](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/13034208) for more information.
---@field bodyStyle? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductAttributesBodyStyleEnum|string The [body style](https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/14157085) of the vehicle.
---@field certifications? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductCertificationList Product Certifications, for example for energy efficiency labeling of products recorded in the [EU EPREL](https://eprel.ec.europa.eu/screen/home) database. For more information, see [Certification](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/13528839).
---@field productWeight? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductWeight The weight of the product in the units provided. The value must be between 0 (exclusive) and 2000 (inclusive).
---@field vin? string The [Vehicle Identification Number (VIN)](https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/14154510) of the vehicle.
---@field lifestyleImageLinks? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.StringList Additional URLs of lifestyle images of the item, used to explicitly identify images that showcase your item in a real-world context. See the [Help Center article](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/9103186) for more information.
---@field productWidth? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductDimension The width of the product in the units provided. The value must be between 0 (exclusive) and 3000 (inclusive).
---@field longitude? number The longitude of the property. The value must be between -180 (inclusive) and 180 (inclusive), up to 6 decimal places.
---@field description? string Description of the item.
---@field fuelConsumptionDischargedBattery? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.FuelConsumption The fuel consumption of the vehicle when the hybrid battery is discharged. See the [Help Center article](https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/15162033) for more information.
---@field costOfGoodsSold? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.Price Cost of goods sold. Used for gross profit reporting.
---@field mobileLink? string URL for the mobile-optimized version of your item's landing page.
---@field pickupCost? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.PickupCost Optional. The [pickup cost](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/16988704) for an item when a customer buys it online and picks it up at a store.
---@field variantOptions? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.VariantOptionList Optional. Contains the [list of all variant-identifying options](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/17085214) of this product.
---@field energyConsumption? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.EnergyConsumption The [energy consumption](https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/14546149) of the vehicle.
---@field mpn? string Manufacturer Part Number ([MPN](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6324482)) of the item.
---@field returnPolicyLabel? string The return label of the product, used to group products in account-level return policies. Max. 100 characters. For more information, see [Return policy label](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/9445425).
---@field vehicleMsrp? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.Price The MSRP (Manufacturer Suggested Retail Price) for the vehicle in its current configuration. See the [Vehicle MSRP](https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/14154171) for more information.
---@field displayAdsTitle? string Title of an item for dynamic remarketing campaigns.
---@field vehicleExpenses? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.Price The miscellaneous expenses like insurance and registration fees of the vehicle. See the [Vehicle expenses](https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/15957154) for more information.
---@field handlingCutoffTimes? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.HandlingCutoffTimeList The handling cutoff times for shipping.
---@field productDetails? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.ProductDetailList Technical specification or additional product details.
---@field fuelConsumption? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.FuelConsumption The [fuel consumption](https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/14543580) of the vehicle.
---@field identifierExists? boolean Set this value to false when the item does not have unique product identifiers appropriate to its category, such as GTIN, MPN, and brand. Defaults to true, if not provided.
---@field canonicalLink? string URL for the canonical version of your item's landing page.
---@field videoLinks? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_products_v1.StringList Optional. A list of video URLs for the item. Use this attribute to provide more visuals for your product beyond your image attributes. See the [Help Center article](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/15216925) for more information.
---@field dateFirstRegistered? string The date the vehicle was first registered. Format: `YYYY-MM`. See the [Date first registered](https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/14546138) for more information.

